==Trivia==
*The [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musket musket] is a muzzle-loaded long gun that appeared as a smoothbore weapon in the early 16th century, at first as a heavier variant of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arquebus arquebus], capable of penetrating [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plate_armour plate armour]. By the mid-16th century, this type of musket gradually disappeared as the use of heavy armour declined, but muskets continued as the generic term for smoothbore long guns until the mid-19th century. In turn, this style of musket was retired in the 19th century when [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rifled_musket rifles] became common.
*The name and description of the [[Cards|card]] is a reference to the classic novel, "''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Three_Musketeers The Three Musketeers]''", with the [[Musketeer]] card being a reference to the fourth Musketeer, D'Artagnan in the same novel.
**In the Spanish language settings of the game, the Three Musketeers' name translates to "Musketeer Trio".
*The Three Musketeers is the most expensive card in the game, and subsequently, the most expensive {{Rarity|Rare}} card, and most expensive [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] card in the game, costing 9 [[Elixir]].
*The Three Musketeers are 1 of 23 cards that has had its Elixir cost changed, the others being [[Bomber]], [[Fire Spirit]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Cannon]], [[Mortar]], Musketeer, [[Heal]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Furnace]], [[Elixir Collector]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Electro Giant]], [[Bowler]], [[Goblin Barrel]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], [[Rage]], [[Fisherman]], [[Monk]]  and the [[Void]].
**The Three Musketeers, the Royal Recruits, the Elixir Collector, Monk and the Void are the only cards whose Elixir cost was increased.
**The Three Musketeers' Elixir cost has changed more than any other card, with a total of 3 times.
*The Three Musketeers are unavailable in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]]. More specifically:
**It is 1 of 9 cards that is unavailable in Triple Draft, the others being [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Clone]], [[Mirror]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Mighty Miner]], and the Monk.
*Using the Musketeer card to summon 3 Musketeers would cost 12 Elixir, whereas using the Three Musketeers card to summon 3 Musketeers costs 9 Elixir.

